Spec: Actions

Platform: Rust/Kubernetes

Purpose:
  Run the plugin's active verbs. The mutating trio (@run_jukebox_scan, @run_instance_scan,
    @run_upgrade) talks straight to the apiserver — one force annotation on the target, then
    polling the operator-recreated @Job while UID-tracking so a stale terminal job never counts
    as the new one — and @run_diagnostic plus the four single-item verbs reuse the ./transport.rs
    fetch layer, with @build_bundle archiving. This file is also the plugin's only deadline host
    (`--timeout` is polled here and nowhere else — never on fetches, per ./transport.sdd), owner
    of the stdout/stderr line contract, and of the exit posture handed to ./main.rs through
    @anyhow::Result: @Ok → exit `0`, @Err → `Error:` on stderr exit `1`.

Owns:
  ./actions.rs

References:
  ./cli.sdd — every input shape: @InstanceKindInfo rows feeding the job name `type_label` and
    the `--vynil-namespace`/`--timeout` values (scan default `90`, upgrade `300`, `0` accepted
    — its meaning is frozen here, `[?]` below), `-w` on @UpgradeArgs only (scans always wait),
    @InstanceVerb::as_item routing, the `__complete`-adjacent globals `-n`/`--context` staying
    @None until this file defaults them, and direct mode parse-restricted to read verbs so
    scan/upgrade are aggregation-only.
  ./transport.sdd — @make_client, @get_item (total: its status-`0` `DIAG-ERR:` sentinel is the
    lane @run_item bails on while the bundle summary misses it, shared `[?]`), @read_sa_token
    called only from @transport_mode, @TransportMode built nowhere else, and the finding that
    `--timeout` never reaches either fetch leg.
  ./items.sdd — @resolve_items fixes @run_diagnostic's fetch order (catalog order, empty
    selection legal, unknown/`""` names already dropped).
  ./bundle.sdd — @build_bundle consumes (item, @GetResult) pairs in delivered order; the
    `>=400`-only `error_items` filter that @run_diagnostic prints verbatim, and @run_item's
    stricter `>=400 || == 0` posture, are the same undecided asymmetry.
  ../common/src/jukebox.sdd — the @JukeBox the annotation rides: cluster scope, kind
    `JukeBox`, plural `jukeboxes`, group `vynil.solidite.fr` — exactly the coordinates
    @vynil_api_resource hardcodes for the scan lane.
  /operator/src/jukebox.sdd — the force-scan consumer: value `true`/`""` = full rescan, else the
    verbatim `SCAN_PACKAGE` filter; terminal `scan-{box}` @Job foreground-deleted then recreated;
    annotation removed only after successful create — so any wait failure here still leaves a
    live trigger and a pending annotation.
  /operator/src/instance_common.sdd — the force-reinstall consumer keyed on presence alone (the
    hardcoded value `"true"` is decorative), removing the annotation then
    @delete_job_and_wait + @upsert_job of the `{type_label}--{ns}--{name}` install job in the
    operator's own namespace.
  ./main.rs — spec-pending caller: @run_jukebox / @run_instance dispatch only, and the @Err →
    `Error:` stderr + exit `1` @anyhand::Result termination is its @anyhow::Result handling;
    parse errors exit `2` (./cli.sdd) and never enter this file.
  ./completion.rs — @vynil_api_resource's second caller (@list_names builds the same
    @ApiResource from its own kind table).

Depends on:
  kube `3.1.0` — @Client (@default_namespace), @api::@Api (@all_with, @namespaced,
    @namespaced_with, @get, @get_opt, @patch), @DynamicObject, @Patch::Merge over
    @PatchParams::@default, @ListParams::@labels, @discovery::@ApiResource.
  k8s-openapi — @batch::@v1::@Job and @core::@v1::@Pod read models (conditions, container env,
    pod phase).
  @tokio::time::@sleep over private @POLL_INTERVAL; @std::time::@Instant/Duration — the whole
    wait arithmetic; @std::collections::@HashMap, @std::io::Write, @std::path::@PathBuf.
  @anyhow — @Context/@bail for every error lane; @serde_json::@json for the annotation patch;
    @chrono::@Utc::@now for the default bundle name.
  @crate::cli, @crate::items::@resolve_items, @crate::transport, @crate::bundle (./cli.sdd,
    ./items.sdd, ./transport.sdd, ./bundle.sdd).

Exposes:
  @run_jukebox — `pub async fn(&@JukeboxArgs, context: @Option<&@str>) -> @anyhow::Result<@()>`:
    sole entry for the jukebox tree, handles the single @JukeboxVerb::Scan arm by building
    @JukeboxScanArgsRef borrowing the parsed fields.
  @run_instance — `pub async fn`, shape (@InstanceKindInfo, @InstanceArgs, context, namespace
    @Option<&@str>) -> @Result<@()>: resolves the namespace, routes @as_item verbs to
    @run_item before the @UpgradeArgs/@InstanceScanArgs/@DiagnosticArgs match, and parks the
    remaining arms on an @unreachable! guard (Tasks).
  @run_jukebox_scan — same @Result, takes @JukeboxScanArgsRef; called only by @run_jukebox.
  @run_instance_scan / @run_upgrade / @run_diagnostic / @run_item — the per-verb runners, all
    `pub` through `pub mod actions;` (./lib.rs); ./main.rs touches only the two dispatchers.
  @JukeboxScanArgsRef — `pub @Debug` struct of borrowed `package` (@Option<&@str>),
    `vynil_namespace` (&@str), `timeout` (@u64): a reference bundle so @run_jukebox clones
    nothing.
  @vynil_api_resource — `pub(crate) fn(kind: &@str, plural: &@str) -> @ApiResource` pinning
    group `vynil.solidite.fr`, version `v1`, api_version `vynil.solidite.fr/v1` verbatim from
    its callers (the @InstanceKindInfo pair, or the literal `"JukeBox"`/`"jukeboxes"`;
    ./completion.rs supplies its own).
  Private @POLL_INTERVAL (2 s), @JobOutcome (@Complete / @Failed(@String)), @set_annotation,
    @job_uid, @wait_job_recreated, @wait_job_terminal, @job_tag, @transport_mode, @watch_pods —
    observable only through the runners' stdout/stderr and @Result.

Must:
  Cluster mutation is exactly two annotation writes, nothing else: @set_annotation sends a
    @Merge patch carrying a single key under @metadata.annotations (@Patch::Merge is a JSON
    merge patch — Tasks for its doc wording), other annotations merge-patch-survive, the plugin
    never deletes or creates a @Job/@Pod — recreation is /operator/src/jukebox.sdd's and
    /operator/src/instance_common.sdd's, which the module doc acknowledges.
  Trigger first, wait second, never roll back: the annotation is patched before any deadline or
    wait exists, so every subsequent timeout/failure leaves the scan or reinstall running
    cluster-side; the operator removes the annotation only after job creation.
  Freshness is UID-gated: @job_uid snapshots the current `scan-{box}` / install-job UID before
    the annotation; @wait_job_recreated accepts only a job whose UID differs from that snapshot,
    and @None (job absent at snapshot — the first-ever install/scan) accepts whatever job first
    exists, since no UID can match it.
  One deadline serves every phase of a run: @Instant::@now + `--timeout` seconds via
    @checked_add (failure after the annotation already landed — Tasks), shared by the recreate
    wait, the terminal wait and the @watch_pods loop; each loop compares @Instant::@now to that
    deadline after its API observation and before the 2 s @sleep, so `--timeout` `0` is exactly
    one observation per loop (fresh-job races aside).
  Terminal reading is narrow in @wait_job_terminal: a condition with `status` exactly `"True"`
    and `type_` `"Complete"` → success; `"Failed"` → failure carrying the condition `message` or
    the literal `"no message"`; every other condition type or status is ignored, and a job whose
    `status` is absent or which stops answering @get_opt just stays non-terminal until the
    deadline — the polls are by name, not UID, after the recreate gate.
  Scan annotation value is `filter.unwrap_or("true")`: full scans write the literal `"true"`,
    partial ones the `cat[/pkg]` text verbatim — no validation, no trimming, no `""`→`"true"`
    normalization (`scan ''` yields the empty value the operator also reads as full), and the
    operator owns the filter grammar (/operator/src/jukebox.sdd).
  @run_instance_scan reads `.spec.jukebox`, `.spec.category`, `.spec.package` off the fetched
    @DynamicObject in exactly that fail order (`SCAN-ERR-08`/`-09`/`-10`), @as_str only —
    non-string JSON fails the same missing-key error — and composes the filter
    `{category}/{package}`, the category-only form being jukebox-verb-only.
  Names must line up by convention: scan job `scan-{box}`, install job
    `{type_label}--{namespace}--{name}` (instance namespace inside the name), both looked up in
    `--vynil-namespace` — the namespace is assumed to be where the operator places jobs, never
    probed (Tasks).
  @run_upgrade prints `Installing version {TAG}` before any waiting verdict, TAG the first
    container's `TAG` env `.value` on the freshly recreated job — @None (`TAG` absent, a
    `valueFrom` reference, no containers) renders the literal `<unknown>`.
  Non-watch upgrade's only success proof is the recreated job's `Complete` condition; -w swaps
    it entirely for @watch_pods and never consults job conditions or pods in the other mode.
  @watch_pods lists @Pod in `--vynil-namespace` with selector
    `type={type_label},namespace={namespace},instance={name}` every 2 s, prints
    `{name}\t{phase}` (unnamed pods take the empty name, missing status the `"Unknown"` phase)
    only when a pod-name-keyed @HashMap sees a changed phase — the first pass prints every
    pod — and returns @Ok once at least one pod was ever seen (map non-empty) and none of the
    currently listed pods sits outside `Succeeded`/`Failed`; reaching the deadline instead
    prints `UPG-ERR-09: watch timed out (pods may still be progressing)` to stderr and still
    returns @Ok.
  @transport_mode dispatches on `--server-url` presence alone: @Some → @TransportMode::Direct
    storing the verbatim URL, the verbatim `--token` or the @read_sa_token fallback (failure =
    `DIAG-ERR-01` — direct-only, out-of-cluster users without `--token` die here), `insecure`
    copied; @None → @TransportMode::@Aggregation carrying `--context` and nothing else, so
    `--token`/`--insecure` are accepted by clap and silently ignored, and the label
    `"direct"`/`"aggregation"` returned with the mode reaches only the bundle manifest.
  @run_diagnostic fetches sequentially in @resolve_items order, eprintln-ing
    `collecting: {item}` before each infallible @get_item and collecting every lane
    failure-free; `-o` text is the output path verbatim (empty string included), else the
    default `{instance name}-diag-{ts}.tar.gz` with `ts` this file's own
    `@Utc::@now` `%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ` stamp (the bundle's internal stamps make three —
    ./bundle.sdd); the summary prints through @BundleSummary fields and joins `error_items`
    with `", "`, so transport-failed `0`-lane items stay invisible here while @run_item fails on
    them (shared posture `[?]`).
  @run_item commits the answer to stdout before judging it: any reported redaction pair first
    eprints `redactions: {d} distinct values, {o} occurrences`, then @write_all of the raw body
    (no newline, no truncation), and only then treats `status >= 400 || status == 0` as a
    `DIAG-ERR-03` bail — a failed item therefore exits `1` with its body already on stdout,
    while `1..399` exits `0`.
  Namespace defaulting is `-n` verbatim (empty string included, validated nowhere) or the
    @default_namespace of a client built just for that lookup — kubeconfig current context, or
    the SA namespace in-cluster — and every runner/loop then builds its own clients via
    @make_client: defaulting + per-action + per-fetch aggregation churn all coexist here.
  Stream posture is fixed: progress chatter (`annotating …`, `waiting for …`, `collecting: …`,
    `building bundle: …`, watch-timeout, redactions) on stderr; artifacts and verdicts
    (`Installing version`, `scan complete: job {ns}/{job} succeeded`,
    `upgrade complete: job {job_name} succeeded` — namespace omitted on this one, unlike the
    scan line —, pod phase lines, bundle summary, item body) on stdout; @Err from any runner is
    ./main.rs's anyhow exit `1` and nothing in this file calls @std::process::@exit.

Must not:
  Deadline a fetch: the transport calls (@get_item legs, @make_client) run undeadlined —
    `--timeout` exists only in the poll/loop signatures above, extending neither
    ./transport.sdd's or ./completion.rs's own timeout story.
  Wait on the annotation's removal: neither `vynil.solidite.fr/force-scan` nor
    `vynil.solidite.fr/force-reinstall` removal is polled; a wait outcome says nothing about the
    annotation's fate.

Accepts:
  Runner arguments as ./cli.sdd parsed them: instance/box names and `-n` any @String verbatim
    (`/` and spaces included — kube-side URI failures become these loops' read errors),
    `--vynil-namespace` verbatim, `--timeout` any @u64 seconds incl. `0` and overflow-prone
    maxima, `-w`/`--insecure` as parsed bools, `package`/`--items`/`-o`/`server_url`/`token`
    verbatim optionals, `context` @None or the verbatim global, and `item` any &str —
    @run_item never checks it against @ALL_ITEMS (server `404` lane, ./transport.sdd).
  @vynil_api_resource accepts any kind/plural pair without validation.

Returns:
  @Ok(()) for: a scan job reaching `Complete`; an upgrade job reaching `Complete` (no -w) or any
    @watch_pods return including its deadline lane; a diagnostic whose bundle was written (zero
    items collected included — the archive ships, the summary prints `Items collected: 0` and
    skips the errors line); an item answer with status `1..399`.
  On-disk/process effects of @Ok: the trigger annotation was written (operator will consume it),
    stdout carries the success lines / bundle bytes / item body per the channel split.

Raises:
  Every failure is an @anyhow::Err with a `ID: text` context or @bail at the call site,
    exiting `1` via ./main.rs: `SCAN-ERR-01`/`UPG-ERR-02`/`INST-ERR-01` for @make_client,
    `SCAN-ERR-02`/`UPG-ERR-03` over `failed to query existing job`, `SCAN-ERR-03`/`UPG-ERR-04`
    over `failed to annotate {name} with {key}={value}`, `SCAN-ERR-04`/`UPG-ERR-05`
    `timed out waiting for job {name} to be (re)created`, `SCAN-ERR-05`/`UPG-ERR-06`
    `timed out waiting for job {name} to finish`, `SCAN-ERR-06`/`UPG-ERR-07`
    `{scan,install} job {name} failed: {msg}`, `SCAN-ERR-07` `failed to read instance`,
    `SCAN-ERR-08`/`-09`/`-10` `instance spec has no .spec.{jukebox,category,package}`,
    `SCAN-ERR-09`/`UPG-ERR-09` `timeout overflow` (both ids doubled — Tasks), `UPG-ERR-08`
    `failed to list pods`, `DIAG-ERR-01` no-token-and-no-SA-token, `DIAG-ERR-02`
    `failed to write item to stdout`, `DIAG-ERR-03` `item '{item}' returned status {status}`.
  Poll-loop read failures inside @wait_job_recreated/@wait_job_terminal carry only the
    context-free `failed to query job` (no id — Tasks).
  @build_bundle's errors (./bundle.sdd: IO/serde/tar, and @item_path's unreachable panic)
    travel @run_diagnostic's `?` untouched, unwrapped by any actions.rs id.
  Panic lane: the @unreachable!("item verbs handled above") arm in @run_instance aborts if
    @as_item and @InstanceVerb ever drift (Tasks).

Handles:
  Recreate-gate lanes: absent job at snapshot (@None) → first job seen wins; same-UID job →
    keep polling (a force trigger the operator has not acted on yet is indistinguishable from a
    slow reaction until the deadline); job vanishing mid-@wait_job_recreated → treated as
    not-yet-recreated, polls continue.
  `Complete`/`Failed` at `status` `"False"`, `Suspended`/`FailureTarget`-style conditions and
    condition-less statuses → non-terminal, wait continues.
  @watch_pods empty-selector-match loops the whole deadline then ends @Ok; a pod disappearing
    from later listings stops counting as pending (surviving terminal pods finish the watch,
    an all-gone pass with history also returns @Ok); phase regression under a reused name
    re-prints as a change.
  Upgrade TAG reading from a template whose `TAG` env uses @valueFrom → `<unknown>`, no error.
  Direct mode with `--server-url=` (empty @Some) → every fetch answers the `0` sentinel, so
    @run_item prints `DIAG-ERR: …` then bails `DIAG-ERR-03 … status 0` while `diagnostic`
    bundles it silently — the asymmetry in one command pair.
  @run_diagnostic's unmatched `--items` → zero `collecting:` lines, still a shipped bundle plus
    summary; `-o ""` → path handed to @build_bundle verbatim (writer's @File::create verdict).

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the scan lane end to end: trigger annotation value/ordering, UID freshness gate,
      `Complete`/`Failed`/`no message` lanes, stderr progress lines, stdout success line — zero
      tests exist in this file (no `#[cfg(test)]` module) and every scenario
      below is unmapped.
  [ ] Cover partial-scan filter verbatim passthrough (`dev/code-server`, category-only, `""`,
      the `true` collision) and @run_instance_scan's `.spec` extraction order incl. the
      non-string-value error lane (`SCAN-ERR-07..10`).
  [ ] Cover timeout semantics: `--timeout` `0` single-observation → `SCAN-ERR-04`/`UPG-ERR-05`,
      shared-deadline exhaustion across recreate+terminal, overflow bail after the annotation
      — none exercised; needs an apiserver fake or injected-clock seams (./transport.sdd notes
      the empty dev-dependencies).
  [ ] Cover upgrade non-watch: job name formula, `Installing version {TAG}`/`<unknown>`,
      `UPG-ERR-07` with the condition message, the namespace-omitted success line.
  [ ] Cover @watch_pods: change-only tab-separated phase lines, first-pass full print,
      all-`Failed` exit `@Ok`, pod-vanished-as-terminal, empty-list-to-deadline @Ok with the
      stderr note, and the never-inspected job conditions posture.
  [ ] Cover @transport_mode legs: `--token` verbatim, @read_sa_token fallback and
      `DIAG-ERR-01`, aggregation ignoring token/insecure, context-only-in-aggregation.
  [ ] Cover @run_diagnostic collection: catalog-order fetches, default `{name}-diag-{ts}` name,
      the four-line summary shape, error-line join, zero-item bundle, and pass-through of
      @build_bundle errors.
  [ ] Cover @run_item: body-before-verdict (stdout already written on the `DIAG-ERR-03`/`0`
      lanes), `1..399` @Ok, redactions stderr line, `DIAG-ERR-02`.
  [ ] Cover @run_instance: `-n` verbatim vs @default_namespace fallback (extra client build),
      @as_item routing before the verb match.
  [?] `--timeout` `0` + one shared deadline across all phases + no deadline on fetches: the
      whole timeout contract is emergent from the loop shape — freeze it here (and settle the
      ./cli.sdd `[?]` that delegated `0` to this file; ./transport.sdd denies reads were ever
      covered).
  [?] Error-id hygiene vs the root rule: `SCAN-ERR-09` is both `timeout overflow` and
      `no .spec.category`, `UPG-ERR-09` serves an @Err id and a stderr notice at once, and
      `failed to query job`/`failed to annotate {name} …` carry no id at all — renumber or
      exempt.
  [?] @watch_pods can never report failure: all-`Failed` pods, vanished pods and the deadline
      all exit `0`, and job conditions are not consulted in -w mode — decide whether upgrade
      `-w` owes a non-zero exit on a failed install.
  [?] The deadline (and its overflow @Err) is computed after the trigger annotation is already
    written: a huge `--timeout` fails with the scan already running — move the check earlier or
      accept.
  [?] @run_item's `status == 0` bail vs the bundle/diagnostic silence on the same lane: pick
      the canonical posture once (./transport.sdd and ./bundle.sdd `[?]`s).
  [?] @set_annotation's doc says strategic merge patch; the code is @Patch::Merge (JSON merge
      patch) — fix the comment, since CRDs cannot take strategic merge anyway.
  [?] @unreachable! in @run_instance panics on future @InstanceVerb drift instead of a compile
      error: make the match exhaustive and drop @as_item's double role, or keep the runtime
      guard.

Done when:
  Every Scenario maps to passing tests, each `[?]` above is a recorded decision, and
    `cargo test -p kubectl-vynil`, clippy and fmt stay green.

Scenario: a full scan annotates then polls a fresh job
  Given box `home` with no prior job, `--vynil-namespace vynil-system --timeout 90`
  When @run_jukebox_scan annotates `vynil.solidite.fr/force-scan` to the literal `true` and the
    operator later creates `vynil-system/scan-home`
  Then stderr carries `annotating jukebox home with force-scan=true` and
    `waiting for scan job vynil-system/scan-home ...`, the wait accepts the job because the
    snapshot UID is @None, and a `Complete`/`True` condition yields exit `0` with stdout
    `scan complete: job vynil-system/scan-home succeeded`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: scan filters and failure message lane
  Given `box home scan dev/code-server` and, in another run, a scan job answering a
    `Failed`/`True` condition
  When each resolves
  Then the annotation value is the verbatim `dev/code-server` (empty or `true` positionals send
    those texts, never `true`-normalization), and the failed job exits `1` with
    `SCAN-ERR-06: scan job scan-home failed: BackoffLimitExceeded` — or `no message` when the
    condition message is @None
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: instance scan composes its filter from the spec triple
  Given a `vsi -n kydah-core reloader scan` whose instance `.spec` reads
    `jukebox: kydah-core`, `category: core`, `package: reloader`
  When @run_instance_scan runs
  Then the filter is `core/reloader` against box `kydah-core`, and a spec missing `jukebox`
    (or holding a non-string one) fails `SCAN-ERR-08` before the category/package checks
    (`SCAN-ERR-09`/`-10`) fire
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: a same-UID job is stale
  Given a terminal `scan-home` job captured pre-annotation, deadline not reached
  When @wait_job_recreated keeps seeing the same UID
  Then it keeps polling every 2 s, and with `--timeout 0` the first such observation is already
    past the deadline → `SCAN-ERR-04: timed out waiting for job scan-home to be (re)created`,
    exit `1`, trigger annotation left in place
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: upgrade announces the version then judges the job
  Given `vti -n app web upgrade` (no -w) and an operator that recreates
    `vynil-system/tenant--app--web` at container env `TAG=v1.2.3`
  When @run_upgrade runs
  Then stdout prints `Installing version v1.2.3` before the verdict, and the new job's
    `Complete` prints `upgrade complete: job tenant--app--web succeeded` (namespace omitted);
    a `Failed` condition instead bails `UPG-ERR-07`, and a missing/`valueFrom` `TAG` prints
    `Installing version <unknown>`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: watch mode reports phases, not failures
  Given `upgrade -w` and pods matching `type=tenant,namespace=app,instance=web` transitioning
    `Pending` → `Running` → `Failed`
  When @watch_pods polls
  Then each change prints one `{name}\t{phase}` line (first pass prints all listed pods), the
    run returns @Ok exit `0` once every listed pod is `Succeeded`/`Failed` — a fully `Failed`
    set included — a pod vanishing from later listings stops counting as pending, and an
    empty-selector match after the deadline prints
    `UPG-ERR-09: watch timed out (pods may still be progressing)` then exits `0` anyway
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: diagnostic collects in catalog order and summarizes
  Given `vsi reloader diagnostic` with `-o /tmp/b.tgz` absent and items resolving to all nine
  When @run_diagnostic runs
  Then stderr shows `collecting: clusterinfo` … one per item in @ALL_ITEMS order then
    `building bundle: {name}-diag-{ts}.tar.gz` (default name with this file's own stamp), and
    stdout the summary block `Bundle written to:` / `Items collected: 9` /
    `Redactions: {d} distinct values, {o} occurrences` / `Items with errors: state, agentlog`
    only when the summary's `>=400` list is non-empty — an item that answered the `0` sentinel
    is absent from that line
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: a single item prints its body before failing
  Given item `agentlog` answering `500`, and a variant answering the `0` `DIAG-ERR:` sentinel,
    and a `200` carrying a redaction header
  When @run_item runs each
  Then stdout receives the raw body bytes verbatim in all three, stderr carries the redactions
    line only for the header case, failures exit `1` with
    `DIAG-ERR-03: item 'agentlog' returned status {500|0}` written after the body is already
    out, statuses `1..399` exit `0`, and a closed stdout fails `DIAG-ERR-02` instead
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: direct mode without a token falls back to the SA file
  Given `--server-url https://diag.internal --token ""` vs no `--token` at all vs no
    `--server-url`
  When @transport_mode runs each
  Then the first goes @TransportMode::@Direct with the empty token stored verbatim, the second
    tries @read_sa_token and its unreadable path yields `DIAG-ERR-01` before any fetch or
    `collecting:` line, and the third selects aggregation+label `"aggregation"`, discarding any
    `--token`/`--insecure` silently — and `--server-url=` (empty @Some) still selects direct
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: namespace defaulting and item routing come from the dispatchers
  Given `vsi reloader agentlog` with and without `-n`
  When @run_instance resolves the namespace
  Then `-n` is used verbatim (empty included), its absence builds a throwaway client for
    @default_namespace (kicking `INST-ERR-01` when no cluster is reachable) and only then
    @as_item routes to @run_item — whose aggregation fetches rebuild the client per item
    regardless
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  job names: box `home` → `scan-home`; instance `web` in `app` under @TENANT_INSTANCE →
    `tenant--app--web`, both looked up inside `--vynil-namespace`
  watch line shape: `{pod name}\t{phase}`; bundle default name `reloader-diag-20260628T140512Z.tar.gz`
  error text shapes: `SCAN-ERR-06: scan job scan-home failed: …`,
    `UPG-ERR-05: timed out waiting for job tenant--app--web to be (re)created`,
    `DIAG-ERR-03: item 'agentlog' returned status 0`
  annotation values: full `true`, partial `core/reloader` (instance), `dev/code-server` or
    bare `dev` (jukebox positional, verbatim)
